{
 "result": "maze.py is a padded-grid, level-synchronous BFS. It reads the grid from stdin, pads it with a wall border so neighbour lookups need no bounds checks, and uses one visited bytearray seeded from the '#' cells. It prints the shortest 4-neighbour S-to-E distance, or -1 if there is none. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78), and assay accepted it with baseline 2.458 and 2.2% noise. The variant that replaced the per-cell deque version measured +38% (3.431 vs 2.479). Remaining risk: hidden inputs with unusual shapes were not tested beyond the samples.",
